        '`build --dry-run` shows the diff, and `build` writes four files next to the spec saved by `design`: `AGENTS.md` (48 lines), the `harness-maintenance` skill in `.agents/skills`, a seeded `docs/agent/decisions.md` log and the lock. Finally `check` confirms that the scripts in `AGENTS.md` exist and that the generated files match the spec, and reminds you that the five “ask before” rules are instructions only. `check --run` would also run the configured commands: it prints them, the directory and a trust warning first, then executes them with your permissions. Below is the complete, unmodified `AGENTS.md` from this example.',
