        'The hardest part is keeping the size in check. `check` reports the number of always-loaded lines and warns when the budget is exceeded (200 by default, following Claude Code’s documentation), but a budget is only a signal. The real discipline is the question at every review: which rule has stopped changing anything? In the spirit of the Harness² paper, change the harness in small steps and keep only what an observation can justify, even if that is just comparing how the agent handles the same task before and after a change. The authors do this automatically on benchmarks; in everyday work, honest observation and a diff in the Git history are enough.',
